      "body": "## Purpose\n\n`test_process_checkpoint` cannot run against hybrid GDN (mamba-family) models:\nthey reject `VLLM_BATCH_INVARIANT=1` at startup\n(`VLLM batch_invariant mode is not supported for GDN_ATTN`), and their batched\ngreedy generation is not run-to-run reproducible, so the test's batched\noutput comparison is unusable for that model family. The CUDA process\ncheckpoint feature therefore has no token-exact regression coverage for GDN\nmodels (the test docstring previously just excluded them).\n\nThis PR makes the test handle hybrid models:\n\n- When `ModelConfig.is_hybrid` is true for the selected model, the test no\n  longer sets `VLLM_BATCH_INVARIANT=1` and compares outputs per request\n  (batch-size-1 generation, which is deterministic for this model family).\n- Non-hybrid models keep the exact previous behavior (batched generation with\n  batch invariance).\n\nCloses #65112\n\n## Test plan\n\nOpt-in GPU test (requires `VLLM_TEST_CUDA_PROCESS_CHECKPOINT=1` and a\ncheckpoint-capable driver), not run in default CI.\n\nVerified on 4×H20 96 GB, driver 580.126.09, torch 2.14.0+cu130, NCCL 2.30.7:\n\n```bash\nVLLM_TEST_CUDA_PROCESS_CHECKPOINT=1 VLLM_TEST_MODEL=Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B \\\n  VLLM_TEST_SLEEP_CYCLES=2 \\\n  pytest tests/basic_correctness/memory/sleep_mode/test_process_checkpoint.py -q\n```\n\n- Hybrid GDN (`Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B`): `[1-p2p]`, `[2-p2p]`, `[4-p2p]` all PASS —\n  per-request outputs verbatim stable across cycles, graph handles identical,\n  zero new captures. (shm cells not exercised for the GDN model.)\n- Non-hybrid (`Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B`), full file (TP1/2/4 p2p + TP2/4 shm, 5/5):\n  PASS via the unchanged batched batch-invariant path.\n\nAdditional scale data with the same protocol (5 cycles): TP2 and TP4 on the\n27B hybrid GDN model all pass with graph identity preserved and zero\nrecaptures.\n\n## Details\n\nThe per-request path loops `llm.generate([prompt], ...)` over the two fixed\nprompts. Everything else in the test (graph identity assertions, replay/capture\ncounters, sleep/wake order rotation) is unchanged.\n\nNote on the gate: `ModelConfig.is_hybrid` covers all hybrid model families\n(not only GDN — e.g. lfm2, olmo_hybrid). Those families keep working in\nper-request mode (the comparison stays token-exact, just slower), so the\nwider gate is a safe simplification; happy to narrow it to mamba-family\nbackends explicitly if preferred.\n",
